   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a13283b8c6006bf8c461",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": false,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Former user",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a13283b8c6006bf8c461",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Here's a more detailed analysis of the issue:",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "If a datastream is added to an existing object, the following chain of methods gets called:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "1) DefaultManagement.addDatastream() (call to ds.getChecksum())",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "2) Datastream.getChecksum()",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "3) DatastreamManagedContent.computeChecksum()",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "4) Datastream.getContentStreamForChecksum()",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "5) DatastreamManagedContent.getContentStream()",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "6) ManagementModule.putTempStream(Context, InputStream) --> From 5) to 6) an empty context is passed along which causes the pep to deny auth due to an indeterminate result",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "7) DefaultManagement.putTempStream(Context, InputStream)",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "8) DefaultAuthorization.enforceUpload(context)",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "The error happens when DatastreamManagedContent passes an empty context to DefaultManagement.putTempStream(..). The issue is not related to the ExternalContentManager in any way. Fedora 3.2 shows the same behavior. ",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
