    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Full solution for this would be to implement FCREPO-718.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Interim solution is to remove the dependency on API-M putTempStream (in fact this is for user-uploaded content, with timed cleanup of the temp file, which isn't so appropriate for this case) and manage the files directly as temp:// files (in the same manner as temp files are managed eg for ingest, inline binary content managed datastreams etc); then once ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "attrs": {
           "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-718#icft=FCREPO-718"
          },
          "type": "inlineCard"
         },
         {
          "text": " is implemented revisit and handle properly.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "DOManager dCommit will clean up any temp:// file used by a managed datastream, so cleanup will happen as part of current code.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "DatastreamManagedContent then needs to handle file:// (directly reading the file), uploaded:// (again directly from the file), plus remote location and existing content location as per current code.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
