 "id": "10648",
 "key": "FCREPO-696",
 "renderedFields": {
  "aggregateprogress": null,
  "aggregatetimeestimate": null,
  "aggregatetimeoriginalestimate": null,
  "aggregatetimespent": null,
  "assignee": null,
  "attachment": [],
  "comment": {
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a13283b8c6006bf8c461",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": false,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Former user",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a13283b8c6006bf8c461",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Here's a more detailed analysis of the issue:<br/>\nIf a datastream is added to an existing object, the following chain of methods gets called:</p>\n\n<p>1) DefaultManagement.addDatastream() (call to ds.getChecksum())<br/>\n2) Datastream.getChecksum()<br/>\n3) DatastreamManagedContent.computeChecksum()<br/>\n4) Datastream.getContentStreamForChecksum()<br/>\n5) DatastreamManagedContent.getContentStream()<br/>\n6) ManagementModule.putTempStream(Context, InputStream) --&gt; From 5) to 6) an empty context is passed along which causes the pep to deny auth due to an indeterminate result<br/>\n7) DefaultManagement.putTempStream(Context, InputStream)<br/>\n8) DefaultAuthorization.enforceUpload(context)</p>\n\n<p>The error happens when DatastreamManagedContent passes an empty context to DefaultManagement.putTempStream(..). The issue is not related to the ExternalContentManager in any way. Fedora 3.2 shows the same behavior. </p>",
     "created": "31/May/10 5:35 AM",
     "id": "11408",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10648/comment/11408",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "6089a13283b8c6006bf8c461",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": false,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Former user",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a13283b8c6006bf8c461",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "31/May/10 5:35 AM"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Full solution for this would be to implement \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-718\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-718\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Refactor management of temp and uploaded files\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10315?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-718\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n.</p>\n\n<p>Interim solution is to remove the dependency on API-M putTempStream (in fact this is for user-uploaded content, with timed cleanup of the temp file, which isn't so appropriate for this case) and manage the files directly as temp:// files (in the same manner as temp files are managed eg for ingest, inline binary content managed datastreams etc); then once \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-718\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-718\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Refactor management of temp and uploaded files\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10315?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-718\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n is implemented revisit and handle properly.</p>\n\n<p>DOManager dCommit will clean up any temp:// file used by a managed datastream, so cleanup will happen as part of current code.</p>\n\n<p>DatastreamManagedContent then needs to handle <a href=\"file://\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">file://</a> (directly reading the file), uploaded:// (again directly from the file), plus remote location and existing content location as per current code.</p>",
     "created": "09/Jun/10 2:06 PM",
     "id": "11420",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10648/comment/11420",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
